e and measure  cleavage activity accordingly  you see on the left hand side in the  graph that across our tested protein  dosage on the x-axis the activity  between the rule and cts cas9 proteins  are comparable  this result suggests that cts cast 9 was  able to maintain in vitro cleavage  activity across doses relative to the  ruo cas9  next we wanted to confirm the activity  of the cts cas9 protein observe in vitro  and to make sure that it is still  preserved when transferred to a cellular  environment  as mentioned we selected primary t cells  for these experiments as they offer the  appropriate cellular contacts needed for  car t cell therapy development workflow  we selected seven guide rnas targeting  four car t-cell related therapeutic  genes  these guides include those used in  literature as well as some other  in-house selected options  for this experiment we leverage the  standard or small bench top scale neon  electroporation system of 10 microliter  we looked at cell viability and editing  efficiency from the two proteins  when looking at the cell viability shown  on the left hand side here we observed  that both protein yielded high viability  or low toxicity  then we measured the editing efficiency  using next generation sequencing and saw  that both ruo and cts cas9 proteins  perform comparably from a performance  perspective  these results suggest that lcts cas9  proteins have comparable functional  performance relative to the research  grade cast 9 and that the gmp  manufacturing process did not negatively  affect performance  wanting to evaluate the cts cas9  performance further at a larger scale we  also evaluated both proteins at 10x  scale up using the larger neon  electropuration platform of 100  microliter  once again we look at cell viability and  editing efficiency  this time we selected four guide rnas  from the previous seven to do further  analysis  similarly you'll find that the cell  viability shown on the left hand side  once again is